### ==============================================================================
### Cyber-Blog API Integration Test Suite (REST Client / IntelliJ HTTP)
### ==============================================================================
### Variables
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@token = your_jwt_token_here

### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 0. Health & Heartbeat
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 0.1 Ping Health Check
GET {{baseUrl}}/ping

### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 1. Authentication (M2)
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 1.1 Register New User
# @name register
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "nakamoto",
  "password": "SecurePassword123!",
  "email": "nakamoto@bitcoin.org",
  "bio": "Building the trustless monetary system."
}

### 1.2 Login & Obtain JWT Token
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "nakamoto",
  "password": "SecurePassword123!"
}

### 1.3 Get Current User Profile (Protected)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 2. Taxonomy & Series Curation (M5)
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 2.1 Create Category (Protected)
# @name createCategory
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/categories
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "name": "Cryptography & Zero-Knowledge",
  "slug": "cryptography-zk",
  "description": "Explorations in STARKs, SNARKs, and elliptic curve mathematics."
}

### 2.2 List Categories with Post Counts (Public)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/categories

### 2.3 Get Posts by Category Slug (Public)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/categories/cryptography-zk/posts

### 2.4 Create Series Column (Protected)
# @name createSeries
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/series
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "title": "Mastering Go & Distributed Systems",
  "slug": "mastering-go-distributed",
  "description": "From Goroutines and memory layout to Paxos and Raft consensus.",
  "cover_image": "https://pub-xxx.r2.dev/covers/go-series.png"
}

### 2.5 List All Series (Public)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/series

### 2.6 Get Series Outline & Ordered Chapters (Public)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/series/mastering-go-distributed

### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 3. Post Management & CRUD (M3)
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 3.1 Create Post Chapter 1 in Series (Protected)
# @name createPost1
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/posts
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "title": "Chapter 1: Memory Layout and Escape Analysis",
  "slug": "go-memory-escape-analysis",
  "summary": "Deep dive into stack vs heap allocation in Go 1.27.",
  "content": "### Memory Layout\nWhen a variable escapes to the heap...",
  "category_id": 1,
  "series_id": 1,
  "order_index": 1,
  "published": true
}

### 3.2 Create Standalone Post (Protected)
# @name createPost2
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/posts
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "title": "Understanding Zero-Knowledge Rollups",
  "summary": "Validity proofs vs Fraud proofs explained simply.",
  "content": "Zero-Knowledge Rollups batch multiple transactions...",
  "category_id": 1,
  "published": true
}

### 3.3 List Posts with Pagination (Public)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/posts?page=1&pageSize=10

### 3.4 Get Post Detail by ID (Public)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/posts/1

### 3.5 Update Post (Protected - Author Only)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/posts/1
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "title": "Chapter 1: Memory Layout and Escape Analysis (Revised)",
  "content": "### Memory Layout (Updated)\nExpanded benchmarks and gc flags."
}

### 3.6 Delete Post (Protected - Author Only)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/posts/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 4. Comment Interactions (M4)
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 4.1 Post a Comment on Article (Protected)
# @name createComment
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/posts/1/comments
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "content": "Incredible explanation! The stack allocation benchmarks are crystal clear."
}

### 4.2 List Comments for an Article (Public)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/posts/1/comments

### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 5. Media Storage & Cloudflare R2 (M6)
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 5.1 Request Presigned Upload URL (Protected)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/media/presign
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "filename": "post-cover-banner.webp",
  "content_type": "image/webp"
}

### 5.2 Server Direct Multipart Upload (Protected)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/media/upload
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=WebAppBoundary

--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="sample.png"
Content-Type: image/png

< ./sample.png
--WebAppBoundary--

### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 6. Course Homework Backward Compatibility Routes (/api/*)
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 6.1 Legacy Register
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "student_01",
  "password": "Password123!",
  "email": "student01@school.edu"
}

### 6.2 Legacy Login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "student_01",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 6.3 Legacy List Posts
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/posts

### 6.4 Legacy Create Post (Protected)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/posts
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "title": "Legacy Post from Homework Route",
  "content": "Content submitted via legacy /api/posts route."
}

### 6.5 Legacy List Comments
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/posts/1/comments

### 6.6 Legacy Create Comment (Protected)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/posts/1/comments
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "content": "Comment submitted via legacy /api/posts/1/comments."
}
